    "id": "redis-course",
    "slug": "redis",
    "title": "Redis — From Beginner to Professional Practice",
    "description": "A visual-first course that follows the attached 24-module, 202-lesson Redis curriculum from fundamentals through data types, application patterns, operations, resilience, security, and professional readiness.",
    "category": "Databases and Infrastructure",
    "level": "Beginner to Professional",
    "sort_order": 36,
    "version_scope": "Reference baseline checked on 2026-10-20 against current Redis documentation. Examples focus on Redis command concepts; JSON, Search, Time Series, probabilistic structures, vector sets, and Arrays vary by version and hosting product. Redis Arrays are documented for Redis Open Source 8.8.0 and later, while vector sets begin in Redis Open Source 8.0. Verify command compatibility against the exact server/service used for a lab.",
    "audience": [
      "students and beginners",
      "backend developers",
      "software engineers",
      "database administrators",
      "DevOps and platform engineers"
    ],
    "prerequisites": [
      "Basic computer concepts and command-line familiarity are recommended.",
      "Introductory programming knowledge is useful for client-library lessons; earlier lessons do not require a particular language.",
      "Practice only with a local or authorized Redis development instance; never expose an unauthenticated Redis service to the public internet."
    ],
    "estimated_workload_hours": 65,
    "lesson_count": 202,
    "module_count": 24,
    "learning_outcomes": [
      "Install, configure and verify a development Redis server and CLI.",
      "Choose and use Redis keys, expiration, strings, hashes, lists, sets, sorted sets, streams and supported specialized data types.",
      "Design cache-aside, session, counter, leaderboard, rate-limit and messaging workflows with explicit correctness boundaries.",
      "Integrate Redis clients using secure configuration, connection reuse, batching and appropriate retry behavior.",
      "Explain persistence, replication, Sentinel, Cluster, memory management, security and production troubleshooting trade-offs.",
      "Verify version/provider capabilities and document operational assumptions before deploying a Redis-backed feature."
    ],
